MANUSCRIPT FINALIZATION, COMPLIANCE, AND RNAAS SUBMISSION
Hours Worked: 11 hours

This phase encompassed the complete preparation, verification, compliance checking, and successful submission of the MW–M31 Research Note to Research Notes of the American Astronomical Society (RNAAS).

Work performed included:

Journal compliance verification

Carefully reviewed RNAAS author guidelines, including:

1500-word total limit (including abstract, captions, references)

Single-figure restriction (no tables)

First-person style rules for single-author papers

Non–peer-reviewed, rapid-publication nature of RNAAS

Verified manuscript suitability for RNAAS (incremental methodological contribution rather than novel theory).

LaTeX class and formatting validation

Confirmed correct use of \documentclass[RNAAS,twocolumn]{aastex631}.

Ensured proper two-column formatting and spacing consistent with RNAAS.

Adjusted column separation and figure placement to maximize figure visibility while remaining compliant.

Verified that the figure appears large and legible on its own page in the compiled PDF.

Figure handling and diagnostics

Debugged figure-related issues, including:

Two-column figure* behavior

Placement relative to section breaks

Ensuring the figure caption fit within RNAAS constraints

Verified that the figure rendered correctly in both Overleaf and the AAS auto-compiled submission PDF.

Warning triage and acceptance

Investigated Overleaf warnings (e.g., underfull \hbox messages).

Determined these were cosmetic line-breaking warnings with no effect on output quality or journal acceptance.

Confirmed that no fatal or submission-blocking LaTeX errors were present.

Bibliography integrity checks

Reviewed BibTeX file for:

Correct journal names and formatting

Software citations (NumPy, matplotlib, Python, Jupyter)

ADS-compatible astronomy references

Verified that:

Bibliography compiled correctly into the PDF

Absence of .bib file from the visible submission file list was expected behavior (bibliography embedded into compiled PDF by the portal).

Submission portal metadata completion

Correctly populated all required submission fields:

Topical corridor: Galaxies and Cosmology

Ethics statement acknowledgment

Funding body: No

MAST data: No

IPAC data: No

Confirmed accuracy of title, abstract, author information, and affiliation.

Unified Astronomy Thesaurus (UAT) classification

Selected and curated an appropriate UAT concept list:

Milky Way Galaxy

Andromeda Galaxy

Galaxy dark matter halos

Galaxy mergers

Galaxy dynamics

Galaxy structure

Computational methods

Ensured the list balanced completeness with concision and matched the scientific scope of the manuscript.

Digital assets declaration

Confirmed absence of:

Machine-readable tables

Figure sets

Animated or interactive figures

External datasets requiring DOI citation

Left Digital Assets section appropriately empty, consistent with a single static figure RNAAS note.

Final compiled-PDF review

Conducted a full visual inspection of the auto-generated submission PDF:

Verified title page formatting

Confirmed abstract length and placement

Checked math rendering, symbols, and typography

Confirmed figure numbering, caption text, and references

Ensured no truncation, spacing errors, or formatting anomalies.

Final approval and submission

Approved the compiled manuscript after confirming full compliance.

Submitted the Research Note successfully through the AAS portal.

Verified that all required submission checkpoints were completed and acknowledged.

Outcome:
The manuscript was submitted in a fully compliant, publication-ready form with no outstanding technical, formatting, or policy issues. This phase finalized the project for archival publication and ADS indexing.
